message.text:
generalized catchup logic has not yet been implemented for each indexer stream. It is simply orchestrating the following steps:

1. get previous block height that was persisted.
2. spin up live block subscription.
3. use first block from live subscription as anchor height.
4. keep buffering the blocks from live subscription.
5. catchup from previous block height to anchored block height.
6. then start from buffered blocks and go all the way till we get to live subscription blocks.

So we can have something in the form of the following psuedocode:
```
run_stream(stream: ChainStream) {
    task = spawn({
        let buf_stream = stream.livestream().await;
        let anchor_height = buf_stream.initial().await;
        stream.catchup(anchor_height).await;

        buf_stream.run()
    })

    // ...
    // process next_event loop
    loop { stream.next_event() }
}

ChainStream {
    const CHAIN: Chain

    next_event() -> ChainEvent
    livestream() -> ChainBufferedStream
    catchup(BlockHeight) emits ChainEvent
}

ChainBufferedStream {
    initial() -> BlockHeight
    run() -> Cancellable emits ChainEvent
}
```

Design this feature and write it to `.planning/PLAN.CATCHUP.md`. List each task inside the plan as well. Ask clarifying questions if there are things that are not quite correct or some pieces are missing once you've seen more of the codebase

